<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24"
    android:tint="#FFFFFFFF">
    <!--
      A pulse shard, drawn for this application. Notification icons are drawn by
      the system as an alpha silhouette, so the whole mark is white on
      transparent and carries no colour of its own.

      Two things it deliberately is not. It is not a flame: the Material
      "whatshot" path is what a shell of this lineage ships by default, and the
      same twelve curves then sit in several unrelated applications at once,
      which is a comparison anyone can run. And it is not the launcher mark
      either — that one is a coin ring crossed by a waveform, and a status bar
      showing a shrunken copy of the launcher icon says nothing the icon did
      not already say.

      The shape reads at the 18×18 the status bar actually gives it: one solid
      body with a facet cut out along its axis, and a chip broken off at the
      lower left. Corners are eased with quadratics so the tips do not alias
      into grey mush at that size.
    -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF"
        android:fillType="evenOdd"
        android:pathData="M12.1,1.9
                          Q12.6,1.9 12.95,2.4
                          L19.3,8.2
                          Q19.75,8.65 19.6,9.25
